{
 "$comment": "Capability contracts (Phase 008 §5.2) for the capabilities registered in registries/capability-registry.json (ids and names are read from the seed). Ports are typed by registered constructs (concept aliases C-nn, or the entry model of a registered registry) — never by storage type (V-CB-03). A consumed port not produced inside a composition must be 'contextProvided' or 'optional' (V-CM-04); a produced port not consumed must be 'terminal' (V-CM-05). 'handler' names the platform runtime operation family that exercises the capability; operations name the governed actions evaluated before execution (UCL-G01). serviceLevels are Measurements with units (Phase 008 §10). Ports marked optional are resolved by canonical identity when no capability in the composition produces them (for example an offer over an exchangeable registered elsewhere).",
 "defaults": {
  "serviceLevels": [
   {
    "metric": "latency-p95",
    "magnitude": 0.25,
    "unit": "s",
    "uncertainty": 0.025
   }
  ]
 },
